========================================================================================================
  V7  WHAT WOULD HAVE TO IMPROVE FOR THIS TEST TO DECIDE THE FORK
========================================================================================================

  |S_MG - S_MI(algebraic)| = 0.0121.  A 3-sigma discrimination needs sigma(S) <= 0.0040, i.e. 29.9x better than today's 0.1208.
  sigma(S)/S adds in quadrature over  Sigma_dyn (12.8%), the baryon SHAPE (13.8%) and V_c^2/R0 (3.1%), so EVERY term would have to fall below 0.63%.  Concretely:
      Sigma_1.1(R0) known to +- 0.42 Msun/pc^2 -- today the four published values SPAN 18.5;
      the disc scale length, bulge mass and gas profile good enough to fix Q to 0.63% -- today 13.4%.
  [PASS] V7a the required precision on Sigma_1.1 is far below the DISAGREEMENT BETWEEN PUBLISHED DETERMINATIONS, so no reduction of statistical error can deliver it -- the obstruction is a systematic one   (need +-0.42, published values span 18.5 Msun/pc^2)
  [PASS] V7b and the baryon SHAPE would have to be pinned an order of magnitude better than any current Milky Way mass model delivers   (need 0.63%, have 13.4% -> a factor 21)

